    <briefdescription>
<para>Represents a JSON Schema tuple-type element with position-dependent validation. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="class_tuple" kindref="compound">Tuple</ref> class models JSON arrays whose elements are heterogeneous and must match different schema definitions depending on their index (“tuple validation” in JSON Schema). Unlike homogeneous arrays, a <ref refid="class_tuple" kindref="compound">Tuple</ref> enforces:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>A fixed length determined by the number of schema items.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Validation of each position using its corresponding <ref refid="class_element" kindref="compound">Element</ref> schema.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>This is used when the schema defines <computeroutput>"<ref refid="class_tuple_1ae268d1c2b878aa72c1d5b094b1a1133d" kindref="member">items</ref>"</computeroutput> as an array instead of an object. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
